  "answer": "## What changed in MUI v5 (Tooltip → Popper props)\n\nIn MUI v5.0.3, `Tooltip` no longer applies `PopperProps` directly. Instead, it introduced **slot-based props** via `componentsProps`. The type for the Tooltip slot is explicit:\n\n- `TooltipProps.componentsProps.popper?: PopperProps & TooltipComponentsPropsOverrides;`  \n  (from `packages/mui-material/src/Tooltip/Tooltip.d.ts`, see the `componentsProps` definition in the excerpt)\n\nSo if you do:\n\n```ts\ncomponentsProps={{ popper: { className: '...' } }}\n```\n\nTypeScript complains because `popper` is typed as **`PopperProps & TooltipComponentsPropsOverrides`**, and **`PopperProps` includes required fields** (e.g. `open` is required in `PopperProps` per the error you posted).\n\nThe relevant Tooltip typing is here:\n\n- `packages/mui-material/src/Tooltip/Tooltip.d.ts` (interface `TooltipProps`):  \n  `componentsProps?: { popper?: PopperProps & TooltipComponentsPropsOverrides; ... }`\n\nAnd `TooltipComponentsPropsOverrides` is empty:\n\n- `packages/mui-material/src/Tooltip/Tooltip.d.ts`:  \n  `export interface TooltipComponentsPropsOverrides {}`\n\nMeaning: there’s no allowance for “partial PopperProps”; it’s exactly `PopperProps` (intersection with an empty interface).\n\n## Why your `className` doesn’t apply (mechanism)\n\n`className` is intended to be provided to the Popper slot **as part of the required `PopperProps` shape** expected by `Tooltip`. Because `PopperProps` requires more than just `className`, the type system prevents passing only `className`.\n\n## What to do\n\nTo satisfy the typing, you must pass a valid `PopperProps` object shape (at least the required fields). Alternatively, if your goal is just styling, consider whether you should be targeting Tooltip’s built-in `classes`/`components`/CSS selectors instead of `componentsProps.popper`.\n\nIf you share your exact `PopperProps` usage (from the sandbox), I can suggest the minimal `componentsProps.popper` object that matches the required `PopperProps` fields.",
